<!-- page.hbs -->
{{!< default}}
{{#post}}
<article class="gh-article {{post_class}}">
    {{#match @page.show_title_and_feature_image}}
    <header class="gh-header gh-canvas">
        <h1 class="gh-title">{{title}}</h1>

        {{#if custom_excerpt}}
            <p class="gh-excerpt">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>
        {{/if}}

        {{#if feature_image}}
            <figure class="gh-feature-image">
                <img src="{{feature_image}}" alt="{{#if feature_image_alt}}{{feature_image_alt}}{{else}}{{title}}{{/if}}" />
                {{#if feature_image_caption}}
                    <figcaption>{{feature_image_caption}}</figcaption>
                {{/if}}
            </figure>
        {{/if}}
    </header>
    {{/match}}

    <style>
        
        .story-box {
            background-color: #fffbf5;
            border-left: 4px solid #8b6f47;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 30px 0;
            font-style: italic;
        }
        .values {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 20px;
            margin: 30px 0;
        }
        .value-item {
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #f4f1ed;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .value-item h3 {
            color: #8b6f47;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            font-size: 1.3em;
        }
        .team-section {
            text-align: center;
            margin: 40px 0;
            padding: 30px;
            background-color: #fffbf5;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .team-section h3 {
            color: #8b6f47;
            font-size: 1.5em;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }
    </style>

    <section class="hero flexy">
        <hgroup class="flexy column">
            <h2>The Heart Behind Aunty Suzy</h2>
            <p>A journey of love, tradition, and community spanning from Palestine to the heart of London.</p>
        </hgroup>
    </section>

    <section class="container">
        <hgroup>
            <h2>Our Story</h2>
        <div class="story-box">
            <p>More than twenty years ago, I arrived in London carrying with me the flavours, traditions, and spirit of my Palestinian heritage. What began as sharing homemade dishes and family recipes with neighbours slowly grew into something much bigger—a way to celebrate Palestinian culture, preserve traditions, and bring people together through food and craft.</p>
        </div>

        <p>Aunty Suzy started as a small passion project in my kitchen, where a handful of handmade items and simple recipes became meaningful connections between communities. Over time, that little kitchen grew into a collection of carefully crafted products—from Labaneh and preserved vegetables to handwoven textiles and embroidered pieces—each one created with genuine care, authenticity, and a commitment to quality.</p>

        <p>Every item in the Aunty Suzy collection carries a story: a memory from home, a technique passed down through generations, or the artistry of Palestinian craftspeople whose work deserves to be seen and celebrated. In a world of mass production, I wanted to create an alternative—a space where handmade goods, creativity, and personal touch truly matter.</p>

        <p>Today, Aunty Suzy is more than a brand. It’s a bridge between cultures, a celebration of heritage, and a way to support artisans and makers who share the same passion for preserving tradition. My hope is that each product brings a little joy, a little beauty, and a little piece of Palestine into your home.</p>
        </hgroup>

        <h2>Our Values</h2>
        <div class="values">
            <div class="value-item">
                <h3>Quality First</h3>
                <p>Every product is inspected carefully to ensure it meets our high standards. We use the best materials available and take pride in our craftsmanship.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="value-item">
                <h3>Sustainable & Ethical</h3>
                <p>We're committed to sustainability. We use eco-friendly materials where possible and aim to minimize our environmental impact.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="value-item">
                <h3>Personal Touch</h3>
                <p>This is a small business, which means you'll get genuine, personal customer service. We care about your experience.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="value-item">
                <h3>Creativity & Innovation</h3>
                <p>We're always exploring new ideas and ways to improve. Your feedback helps us create better products.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <h2>What We Create</h2>
        <p>
            Aunty Suzy offers a diverse range of handmade products across several categories:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
            <li><strong>Food:</strong> Artisan food products made fresh in small batches</li>
            <li><strong>Recipes:</strong> Carefully tested recipes and cooking guides to inspire your kitchen</li>
            <li><strong>Handicrafts:</strong> Hand-crafted items that add beauty to your home</li>
            <li><strong>Art:</strong> Original artwork and creative pieces</li>
            <li><strong>Tickets:</strong> Exclusive access to workshops, classes, and events</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who We're Here For</h2>
        <p>
            Aunty Suzy is for anyone who appreciates quality, authenticity, and the warmth of handmade goods. Whether you're looking for a gift, something special for yourself, or inspiration for your own creative journey, we'd love to help.
        </p>

        <div class="team-section">
            <h3>Made With ❤️</h3>
            <p>Designed and developed by <strong>AbuEin Technologies</strong></p>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9em; margin-top: 10px; color: #999;">
                Building beautiful digital experiences for small businesses
            </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Get In Touch</h2>
        <p>
            I'd love to hear from you! Whether you have questions, feedback, or just want to say hello, feel free to reach out. You'll find all the ways to contact me on our Support page.
        </p>
    </section>

    <div class="gh-content gh-canvas">
        {{content}}
    </div>
</article>
{{/post}}